# Git for Windows sets core.autocrlf=true in its system config; cygwin's git does
# not. Two shells on the same machine therefore commit the same file differently,
# which is how a 54-file CRLF rewrite once landed on top of an 8-file change.
#
# eol=lf rather than text=auto alone: leaving the working tree to core.autocrlf is
# what let the two disagree in the first place. LF in the index and LF on disk,
# whichever git runs.
* text=auto eol=lf
